  </p>

  <p>
    Notice the shape of the real jump in that ladder: it is almost never the entry route alone. It is government
    employment, a clinical certification, or an abroad licence that moves the number — not years of general ward
    duty by itself. Nurses who treat that certification, posting, or licence as a deliberate
    <strong>high-value skill portfolio</strong> move, rather than something to figure out later, are the ones who
    actually reach <strong>high income opportunities</strong> in this field.
  </p>

  <h2 id="scaling">How nurses actually scale their income</h2>

  <p>
    A general ward role has a real, fairly low ceiling on its own. But nursing has genuine headroom to scale toward
