    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="highlight-box highlight-box--amber">
    <p>
      Neither side cancels the other out. The genuine sense of purpose in nursing is real, and so is a genuinely
      understaffed system that puts real pressure on the nurses working inside it — that structural shortage is
      exactly where the field's pay and burnout problem comes from.
    </p>
    <p>
      Going in with accurate expectations about the ratio crisis and the pay curve, not brochure expectations
      about a "noble calling," is what separates people who build a sustainable nursing career from people who
      burn out or leave the profession within the first several years — a well-documented pattern in Indian
      nursing-workforce research.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2 id="own-injury">The occupational-health data nobody mentions</h2>

  <p>
    This is the part most nursing college websites skip entirely, because it does not make for a good admissions
    pitch. It is also useful to understand honestly before you commit years and real fees to this path.
